<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92255" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ῥέᾱ</span></b> , ἡ, 
			Ep.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ῥείη</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Il.
			14.203
		</span></i> (in gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ῥείης</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ῥείας</span>
			), <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Cer.</u>
				442
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Ap.</u>
				93
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ῥέη</span> codd.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Ven.</u>
				43
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				625
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ῥείαν</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				135
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ῥεῖα δ᾽ ὑποδμηθεῖσα</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				453
			</span></i> (but with 
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ῥείη δ᾽ αὖ δμηθεῖσα</span>
			); gen. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ῥείας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					6.219.20
				</span></i>
			 (Antip.); the common form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ῥέα</span> is found in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				15.187
			</span></i>, as a monosyll.; 
				contr.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ῥῆ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pherecyd.Syr.
					9
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ῥέη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Cer.</u>
					459
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				467
			</span></i>:—<u>Rhea</u>, daughter of Uranos and Gaia,
			wife of Cronos, mother of Zeus and the gods, ll. cc. [Derived by
				<i><span class="en">
				Chrysipp.Stoic.
				2.318
			</span></i> from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥέω</span>, because rivers
			flow from Earth.] </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pythag.
			</span></i> name for <i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i>, Anatolius ap.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Theol.Ar.</u>
				12
			</span></i>; also for <i><span class="en">
				23
			</span></i> or <i><span class="en">
				8
			</span></i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				55
			</span></i>.</div>
